From 48fba2bbe393196256a720b0cbe7a7bafc30f02e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:33:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 109/110] Faction warfare

Faction warfare by Crucible's rules (FacWarMgr.h), where the server
only had stubs:
- militias:  a character in an NPC corp enlists at a militia office
  with 0.5 standing to the faction or a Letter of Recommendation;  a
  player corp's CEO or director enlists the corp, which joins at the
  next downtime and leaves at the one after it asks to.  Members whose
  standing drops are warned, then removed.  The Amarr and Caldari
  militias are at war with the Gallente and Minmatar ones, anywhere,
  high security too, without CONCORD
- complexes:  minor, medium and major military complexes in the war
  zones, taken by holding their capture point with no enemy in range.
  They give victory points;  at 200 the system's control bunker can be
  shot, and destroyed it hands the system over at the next downtime.
  The war zone map and militia windows answer from facWarSystems, and
  GMs have /fw
- militia missions from the militia agents (levels 1 to 4, in a system
  the enemy holds), militia ranks by standing, and loyalty points for
  killing enemy militia ships

Fixes rolled in:
- GM commands with an optional number argument left out no longer
  crash the server (Seperator::isNumber() read past the last argument)
- the star map's victory points come from the war zones
